# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the first one is the important one.
#
# Secrets. A `.env`, a token file or a credential copied into a layer stays in
# that layer even if a later instruction deletes it, and anyone who can pull the
# image can read it back. Everything that could hold one is excluded here, and
# the images take their configuration from the environment or a mounted volume.
#
# Size and cache. A virtual environment or a test cache in the context is copied
# to the daemon on every build and invalidates layers for no reason.

# Credentials and local configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.secrets/
**/.secrets/
*.pem
*.key
**/gmail-token.json

# Environments and caches
.venvs/
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Version control and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/

# Nothing an image needs at runtime
tests/
scenarios/
docs/
.github/
*.md
!README.md
